	(10, 1, 13, 'Day 8', 'Backend Service Consolidation & Layered Architecture Review', '{"Day": "Day 8", "Week": "Week 2", "Topic": "Backend Service Consolidation & Layered Architecture Review", "Module": "Java Backend Development", "Source": "PACKT", "Remarks": "Include Modules\nLayered Architecture, ORM Framework and Creating New Property API - 2h 12m\nGET, PUT, PATCH, DELETE Operation on Properties - 44m\nAOP and Error Handling - 46m\nSwagger Automatic API Documentation - 23m\nfrom given course", "Duration": "4:05:00", "Sub Topic": "Consolidating catalog, account, cart and order-tracking REST endpoints into one coherent Spring Boot service\nReviewing layered architecture consistency across all endpoints\nEnd-to-end request tracing from controller to repository\nFinalizing DTO contracts that the Angular client will consume\nReviewing security, validation and error-handling consistency\nPreparing a Postman collection / OpenAPI spec as the frontend contract\nDatabase schema review and migration consistency check\nReadiness check before frontend foundation sessions begin", "Proficiency": "Advanced", "Hands-on Labs": "Case Study – Java Backend Journey Consolidation\nInput: Existing PulseCart controllers, services, repositories and entities from prior Java backend sessions.\nImplement: Consolidate the catalog, account, cart and order-tracking endpoints into one coherent, secured Spring Boot service.\nIntegrate: Combine persistence, validation, security and error handling into one consistent backend.\nValidate: Verify endpoint behavior, security enforcement, and DTO contract stability end-to-end.\nOutput: Consolidated, production-style Spring Boot backend ready to be consumed once the frontend foundation is complete.\nEvidence: Source code, Postman collection/OpenAPI spec, test results and short implementation note.", "Duration (Hrs)": "4", "Published Date": "7/28/22", "Total Duration": "4:05:00", "Course / You tube": "Zero to Hero Java SpringBoot and JPA Mastery with Real Project", "Learning Outcomes": "Consolidate a complete Spring Boot backend journey with reusable controllers, services and repositories ready for frontend consumption.", "Learning Type (SPL / IL)": "SPL", "Customised course names for Skill Assist": "Zero to Hero Java SpringBoot and JPA Mastery with Real Project - Sony Java with Angular"}'),
	(6, 1, 9, 'Day 4', 'REST API Design, Validation, Service Layer Business Logic', '{"Day": "Day 4", "Week": "Week 1", "Topic": "REST API Design, Validation, Service Layer Business Logic", "Module": "Java Backend Development", "Source": "PACKT", "Remarks": "Include Module\nRESTful Web Services with Spring Boot - 4h 45m\nfrom given course", "Duration": "4:45:00", "Sub Topic": "RESTful API design principles: resources, verbs and status codes\nRequest validation with Bean Validation (@Valid, @NotNull, custom validators)\nService-layer business logic separated from persistence and presentation\nDTO/mapper patterns for clean request/response contracts\nConsistent error contracts and problem-detail responses\nAPI versioning strategies\nDesigning endpoints for the PulseCart catalog/cart/order domain\nDocumenting APIs with OpenAPI/Swagger Delivered as an Instructor-Led (IL) session because of its complexity, integration or coordination needs; the mentor also opens with a guided review of the preceding Self-Paced (SPL) day(s) and resolves learner queries from those days before moving into today''s live topic.", "Proficiency": "Advanced", "Hands-on Labs": "Case Study – REST API Design, Validation, Service Layer Business Logic\nInput: PulseCart backend requirements, the agreed data model and existing project baseline.\nImplement: Design validated catalog/cart/order endpoints with a clean service layer and OpenAPI documentation.\nIntegrate: Reuse the same catalog, account, cart and order-tracking journey components/contracts already built in prior sessions.\nValidate: Run the feature, verify expected success/failure behavior and check the relevant integration path.\nOutput: Working REST API Design, Validation, Service Layer Business Logic increment integrated into the continuous PulseCart OneJourney solution.\nEvidence: Source code/configuration, screenshots or test output, and a short implementation note.", "Duration (Hrs)": "4", "Published Date": "6/30/21", "Total Duration": "4