	(7, 1, 10, 'Day 5', 'Spring Security Fundamentals & JWT Authentication', '{"Day": "Day 5", "Week": "Week 2", "Topic": "Spring Security Fundamentals & JWT Authentication", "Module": "Java Backend Development", "Source": "PACKT", "Duration": "4:31:00", "Sub Topic": "Spring Security filter chain and configuration fundamentals\nAuthentication providers and password encoding (BCrypt)\nBuilding a custom UserDetailsService for PulseCart accounts\nJWT structure, signing and stateless authentication for REST APIs\nIssuing and validating JWTs on login and subsequent requests\nRefresh-token concepts and expiry handling\nCORS configuration for Angular client consumption\nTesting authentication flows with Postman and automated tests", "Proficiency": "Basic", "Hands-on Labs": "Case Study – Spring Security Fundamentals & JWT Authentication\nInput: PulseCart backend requirements, the agreed data model and existing project baseline.\nImplement: Implement Spring Security with a custom UserDetailsService and JWT issuance/validation for the PulseCart login flow.\nIntegrate: Reuse the same catalog, account, cart and order-tracking journey components/contracts already built in prior sessions.\nValidate: Run the feature, verify expected success/failure behavior and check the relevant integration path.\nOutput: Working Spring Security Fundamentals & JWT Authentication increment integrated into the continuous PulseCart OneJourney solution.\nEvidence: Source code/configuration, screenshots or test output, and a short implementation note.", "Duration (Hrs)": "4", "Published Date": "8/26/22", "Total Duration": "4:31:00", "Course / You tube": "Practical Bootcamp JWT Authentication with Java and Spring Boot", "Learning Outcomes": "Implement JWT-based authentication for PulseCart using Spring Security.", "Learning Type (SPL / IL)": "SPL"}'),
	(8, 1, 11, 'Day 6', 'Authorization, Role-Based Access Control & API Security Hardening', '{"Day": "Day 6", "Link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e5585jgfTU8\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DadwY18t_Ow", "Week": "Week 2", "Topic": "Authorization, Role-Based Access Control & API Security Hardening", "Module": "Java Backend Development", "Duration": "00:21:29\n\n00:55:42", "Sub Topic": "Role/claim-based authorization on endpoints (@PreAuthorize, method security)\nSecuring sensitive endpoints and restricting unauthorized operations\nDesigning role/permission models for the PulseCart account and order domain\nOAuth concepts and delegated authorization flow at a practical level\nHandling 401/403 responses consistently\nProtecting against common API security risks (mass assignment, over-fetching)\nSecurity-focused code review checklist for REST endpoints\nTesting authorization rules with both valid and invalid roles Delivered as an Instructor-Led (IL) session because of its complexity, integration or coordination needs; the mentor also opens with a guided review of the preceding Self-Paced (SPL) day(s) and resolves learner queries from those days before moving into today''s live topic.", "Hands-on Labs": "Case Study – Authorization, Role-Based Access Control & API Security Hardening\nInput: PulseCart backend requirements, the agreed data model and existing project baseline.\nImplement: Add role/claim-based authorization to account and order endpoints, then verify both authorized and unauthorized access paths.\nIntegrate: Reuse the same catalog, account, cart and order-tracking journey components/contracts already built in prior sessions.\nValidate: Run the feature, verify expected success/failure behavior and check the relevant integration path.\nOutput: Working Authorization, Role-Based Access Control & API Security Hardening increment integrated into the continuous PulseCart OneJourney solution.\nEvidence: Source code/configuration, screenshots or test output, and a short implementation note.", "Duration (Hrs)": "4", "Total Duration": "1:17:00", "Course / You tube": "Spring Security - Method Security Explained | @PreAuthorize, @PostAuthorize\n\nSpring Security JWT Role-Based Authorization Tutorial", "Learning Outcomes": "Enforce role-based authorization and harden PulseCart REST endpoints against common API security risks.", "Learning Type (SPL / IL)": "IL"}'),
	(9, 1, 12, 'Day 7', 'Testing & Data Access Hardening (JUnit, Mockito, Testcontainers)', '{"Day": "Day 7", "Week": "Week 2", "Topic": "Testing & Data Access Hardening (JUnit, Mockito, Testcontainers)", "Module": "Java Backend Development", "Source": "PACKT", "Remarks": "Include Modules\nUnit Test & Different Annotations - 27m\nLifecycle of Test and Assertions - 11m\nWriting Test cases with JUnit 5 - 45m\nWriting Test cases for Controller Layer - 44m\nWriting Test Cases for Converter & Service Layer - 44m\nWriting Test Cases for Exception and Model - 14m\nfrom given course", "Duration": "3:05:00", "Sub Topic": "Unit testing services and controllers with JUnit 5 and Mockito\nIntegration testing with @SpringBootTest and MockMvc\nTesting repositories against an embedded/test database with Testcontainers\nMocking external dependencies and edge-case scenarios\nContract testing between the backend and the Angular client expectations\nLogging and structured error handling for observability\nPerformance basics: connection pooling and N+1 query detection\nValidating API behavior against the PulseCart requirements Delivered as an Instructor-Led (IL) session because of its complexity, integration or coordination needs; the mentor also opens with a guided review of the preceding Self-Paced (SPL) day(s) and resolves learner queries from those days before moving into today''s live topic.", "Proficiency": "Basic", "Hands-on Labs": "Case Study – Testing & Data Access Hardening (JUnit, Mockito, Testcontainers)\nInput: PulseCart backend requirements, the agreed data model and existing project baseline.\nImplement: Add JUnit/Mockito unit tests and MockMvc/Testcontainers integration tests for the catalog and order-tracking endpoints; capture before/after evidence.\nIntegrate: Reuse the same catalog, account, cart and order-tracking journey components/contracts already built in prior sessions.\nValidate: Run the feature, verify expected success/failure behavior and check the relevant integration path.\nOutput: Working Testing & Data Access Hardening (JUnit, Mockito, Testcontainers) increment integrated into the continuous PulseCart OneJourney solution.\nEvidence: Source code/configuration, screenshots or test output, and a short implementation note.", "Duration (Hrs)": "4", "Published Date": "10/26/22", "Total Duration": "3:05:00", "Course / You tube": "Practical Junit & Mockito Test with Java SpringBoot & JPA", "Learning Outcomes": "Harden the Spring Boot backend with unit, integration and contract-level tests.", "Learning Type (SPL / IL)": "IL", "Customised course names for Skill Assist": "Practical Junit & Mockito Test with Java SpringBoot & JPA - Sony Java with Angular"}'),
