	(11, 1, 14, 'Day 9', 'API Documentation & Contract Finalization for Frontend Consumption', '{"Day": "Day 9", "Link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0CSyIBHQy9g", "Week": "Week 2", "Topic": "API Documentation & Contract Finalization for Frontend Consumption", "Module": "Java Backend Development", "Duration": "1:55:00", "Sub Topic": "Finalizing OpenAPI/Swagger documentation for all PulseCart endpoints\nPublishing a stable REST contract for future Angular consumption\nSample request/response payload documentation\nBackward-compatible API evolution practices\nCORS and environment configuration for local frontend development\nPostman collection handoff and API smoke testing\nAligning error-response shapes with expected frontend error-handling behavior\nSign-off checklist before frontend foundation and Angular sessions", "Hands-on Labs": "Case Study – Backend Contract Finalization\nInput: The consolidated PulseCart Spring Boot backend and its OpenAPI/Postman documentation.\nImplement: Finalize and publish a stable, versioned REST contract with sample payloads and CORS configuration for future frontend consumption.\nIntegrate: Align error-response shapes and DTO contracts with the upcoming Foundation and Angular sessions.\nValidate: Smoke-test every endpoint via Postman and confirm the published contract matches actual behavior.\nOutput: A documented, stable Java REST API contract ready for frontend integration.\nEvidence: OpenAPI spec, Postman collection, smoke-test evidence and short implementation note.", "Duration (Hrs)": "4", "Total Duration": "1:55:00", "Course / You tube": "API Documentation Best Practices – Full Course", "Learning Outcomes": "Finalize and document a stable Java REST API contract ready for frontend integration.", "Learning Type (SPL / IL)": "SPL"}'),
	(12, 1, 18, 'Day 10', 'JavaScript (ES6+), TypeScript', '{"Day": "Day 10", "Week": "Week 2", "Topic": "JavaScript (ES6+), TypeScript", "Module": "Foundation", "Source": "PACKT\nPACKT", "Remarks": "Include Modules\nJavaScript basics - 1h 42m\nAdvanced JavaScript topics - 1h 16m\nfrom JavaScript Essentials 2026 - Quickstart Guide for Beginner course\n\nInclude Modules\nVariables and Data Types - 27m\nObjects and Arrays - 16m\nFunctions - 30m\nInterfaces - 28m\nStatic Methods - 8m\nfrom TypeScript for Beginners course", "Duration": "2:58:00\n1:49:00", "Sub Topic": "JavaScript ES6+ syntax: let/const, template literals, destructuring, spread/rest and default parameters\nModules and reusable functions using import/export\nArrays and objects: map/filter/reduce, immutable update patterns and object transformation\nTypeScript primitives, arrays, tuples, enums, unions and literal types\nInterfaces vs type aliases; optional/readonly properties and reusable domain models\nTyped functions, return types, callbacks and basic generic usage\nType narrowing, null/undefined handling and compile-time error interpretation\nOrganizing typed frontend code for maintainability and API consumption", "Proficiency": "Intermediate\nBasic", "Hands-on Labs": "Case Study – JavaScript (ES6+), TypeScript\nInput: PulseCart foundation requirements, the DTO shapes published by the Java backend, and existing project baseline.\nImplement: Create typed product, cart and customer models plus reusable transformation/validation utilities matching the Java backend''s DTO contracts.\nIntegrate: Reuse the same catalog, account, cart and order-tracking journey components/contracts already built in prior sessions.\nValidate: Run the feature, verify expected success/failure behavior and check the relevant integration path.\nOutput: Working JavaScript (ES6+), TypeScript increment integrated into the continuous PulseCart OneJourney solution.\nEvidence: Source code/configuration, screenshots or test output, and a short implementation note.", "Duration (Hrs)": "4", "Published Date": "18-12-2025\n26-10-2020", "Total Duration": "4:47:00", "Course / You tube": "JavaScript Essentials 2026 - Quickstart Guide for Beginners\nTypeScript for Beginners", "Learning Outcomes": "Use modern JavaScript and TypeScript safely to model frontend data that mirrors the Java backend''s DTO contracts.", "Learning Type (SPL / IL)": "SPL", "Customised course names for Skill Assist": "JavaScript Essentials 2026 - Quickstart Guide for Beginners - Sony Java with Angular\nTypeScript for Beginners - Sony Java with Angular"}'),
