	(16, 1, 25, 'Day 14', 'Directives, Data Binding & Custom Directives', '{"Day": "Day 14", "Week": "Week 3", "Topic": "Directives, Data Binding & Custom Directives", "Module": "Angular Frontend Development", "Source": "RADO", "Remarks": "Include module\nUnderstanding the role of Components and Directives - 52m\nTemplates and Data Binding - 1hr 7m\nAngular View Child - 51m\nfrom given course", "Duration": "2:50:00", "Sub Topic": "Structural directives (*ngIf, *ngFor) and attribute directives (ngClass, ngStyle)\nInterpolation, property binding, event binding and two-way binding (ngModel)\nBuilding custom attribute and structural directives for reusable DOM behavior\nPipes: built-in pipes and writing custom pipes for display formatting\nTemplate reference variables and view queries (@ViewChild)\nContent projection basics with ng-content\nApplying directives and binding to the PulseCart catalog/cart components\nDebugging binding and directive issues with Angular DevTools", "Proficiency": "Advanced", "Hands-on Labs": "Case Study – Directives, Data Binding & Custom Directives\nInput: PulseCart frontend requirements, the finalized Java REST contract and existing project baseline.\nImplement: Convert the PulseCart catalog shell into reusable components using directives, data binding and custom pipes for product cards, filters and cart badge.\nIntegrate: Reuse the same catalog, account, cart and order-tracking journey components/contracts already built in prior sessions.\nValidate: Run the feature, verify expected success/failure behavior and check the relevant integration path.\nOutput: Working Directives, Data Binding & Custom Directives increment integrated into the continuous PulseCart OneJourney solution.\nEvidence: Source code/configuration, screenshots or test output, and a short implementation note.", "Duration (Hrs)": "4", "Published Date": "4/14/23", "Total Duration": "2:50:00", "Course / You tube": "Angular 15", "Learning Outcomes": "Apply directives, data binding 